     ddcc is an arbitrary-precision reverse-Polish desk calculator
     with 256 registers, each of which is itself a small stack.
     If _f_i_l_e is given, ddcc reads and executes it first; it then
     reads and executes the standard input.  An arbitrary number
     of commands may appear per line, and commands need not be
     separated by spaces.

     Numbers are pushed onto a value stack; operators pop their
     operands from that stack and push the result.  A number is a
     string of the digits 00 through 99 and the letters AA through
     FF, optionally containing one decimal point; the letters
     stand for the values ten through fifteen regardless of the
     input base currently in effect.  An underscore (_) im-
     mediately before a number makes it negative.  Every value
