     ddcc recognizes the following commands:

     + -  * / % ^
              Pop the top two values, apply addition, subtrac-
              tion, multiplication, division, remainder, or ex-
              ponentiation (in that order), and push the result.
              For ^, the exponent's fractional part, if any, is
              ignored.

     cc        Clear (discard) the entire stack.

     dd        Duplicate the top of the stack.

     ff        Print every register that has a value, followed by
              the entire stack.

     ii        Pop the top of the stack and use its integer part
              as the input base (digits are taken from 00- FF, so
              the input base is normally between 2 and 16).

     II        Push the current input base.

     kk        Pop the top of the stack and use its integer part
              as the scale factor used by division; a negative
              value is rejected and the scale is left at zero.

     KK        Push the current scale factor.

