     On a stack-empty, stack-full, out-of-memory, missing-regis-
     ter-name, negative-scale, or unrecognized-command error, ddcc
     prints a one-line message to the standard error and abandons
     the command it was in the middle of, but continues reading
     input immediately after the offending character.

